itology","topicOriginal":"Medical Parasitology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Cryptosporidium parvum"},{"label":"B","text":"Enterobius vermicularis"},{"label":"C","text":"Adhesive disk ,"},{"label":"D","text":"Hermaphrodite E Cysticercus (cysticerci)"},{"label":"F","text":"Entamoeba histolytica"},{"label":"G","text":"Binary fission"},{"label":"H","text":"Taenia saginata I. Cytokinesis J. Auto infection K. Echinococcus multilocularis L. Echinococcus granulosus M. Taenia solium SHORT ANSWER QUESTIONS:"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Parasitology","displayTopic":"Medical Parasitology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-660f6671e4f5","stem":"Hookworm disease was a major health problem in German and English coal mines in the early 20th century. (3 marks) What is the main pathological problem with this infection? How does one get infected with hookworms? Why this infection was so prevalent in the mines but not in the adjacent city neighborhoods the mines lived in.","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Parasitology","topic":"Medical Parasitology","topicOriginal":"Medical Parasitology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Parasitology","displayTopic":"Medical Parasitology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-1e483ef3abf7","stem":"How Enterobiasis infections diagnosed? (4 marks)","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Parasitology","topic":"Medical Parasitology","topicOriginal":"Medical Parasitology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"_ Cysts in formed stools and trophozoites in diarrhea stools"},{"label":"B","text":"_ Serological tests are useful for the diagnosis of extraintestinal amoebiasis"}],"priority":0,"status":"review","flags":["mcq_missing_options"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Parasitology","displayTopic":"Medical Parasitology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["mcq_missing_options","not_enough_options","prior_structural_review_flag"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-a3cdc3a28958","stem":"You are a doctor in a small town and several children come to your practice with diarrhea with loose, foul smelling stools, some vomiting, nausea, anorexia and complaining abdominal cramps. You do stool examinations and treat them appropriately. Later on in the same week two more children come to see you with the same symptoms. After some questioning you find out that they all go to the swimming pool. (4 marks)","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Parasitology","topic":"Medical Parasitology","topicOriginal":"Medical Parasitology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":". What did you find they had? GIARDIA LAMBLIA"},{"label":"B","text":". How did you treat them? METRONIDAZOLE"},{"label":"C","text":"Is there anything that you can do to control this outbreak -establishment of sanitation to swimming pool -provision of education especially to the children -personal hygiene should be established -establishment of good sewage system"},{"label":"D","text":"What can you recommend to the pool owner to do about -the usual replacement of used water by clean water -he should design the swimming pool into different spaces each person should use its own"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Parasitology","displayTopic":"Medical Parasitology","