","text":"Eggs do not require a period of development in the soil before being ingested."},{"label":"D","text":"eggs are passed in which hatch and reinfect within 2-3 hours by being carried from the anal margin to the mouth"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","subject_needs_classification","subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"1294ed471abe02b9e848165355836e2590ee7430"},{"id":"q-55cf5f53fa01","stem":"Ascaris, Strongyloides, Enterobius, Hookworm are all","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Parasitology","topic":"Medical Parasitology","topicOriginal":"Medical Parasitology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Cestodes"},{"label":"B","text":"Nematodes"},{"label":"C","text":"Trematode"},{"label":"D","text":"Protozoa SECTION II – TRUE/FALSE QUESTIONS, MATCHING AND SHORT ANSWER QUESTIONS TRUE OR FALSE QUESTIONS Write the correct answer in the box, which is either true or false for questions"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Parasitology","displayTopic":"Medical Parasitology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["answer_text_in_option","repeated_question_stem"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"6fda36ea24af307bcaca26d8349fb99c3e31fcc6"},{"id":"q-475d0852098a","stem":"10: (10 marks) (Penalty half a mark for a guess work). . Praziquantel - effective in the treatment of all forms of schistosomiasis, with virtually no side effects T • Oxamniquine - used exclusively to treat intestinal schistosomiasis in Africa and South America • Metrifonate - effective for the treatment of urinary schistosomiasis • Intermediate host; The host occupied by juvenile stages of a parasite prior to the definitive host and in which asexual reproduction often occurs. T • Reservoir host: Refers to a host or carrier that harbors disease-causing organisms, without injury to itself and serves as a source from which other individuals can be infected. T • Definitive host: the host in which the sexual reproduction of a parasite takes place F • Vector: An organism, often an insect or rodent, that carries disease. T • The principal means of acquiring the toxoplasmosis infection is either by ingestion of inadequately cooked meat primarily beef, pork and lamb or by contact with feral or domestic cats. T • Cryptosporidium parvum is a vector borne. F • Balantium coli is a cestode F • Cats are intermediate hosts habor sexual stage for toxoplasma F MATCHING QUESTIONS Match the following by writing the correct letter on the space provided (10 marks each) ____ sporocysts ____ adhesive disk ____ tachyzoites ____Schistosomatidae ____ schizogony","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Parasitology","topic":"Helminthology","topicOriginal":"Helminthology","subtopic":"Schistosomiasis","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"used for attachment by Giardia"},{"label":"B","text":"Gynecophoral canal"},{"label":"C","text":"Toxoplasma gondii SHORT ANSWERS QUESTIONS:"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Parasitology","displayTopic":"Helminthology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-2912e9796443","stem":"Mention three important factors in the transmission cycle of Schistosoma mansoni","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Parasitology","topic"