"Medical Parasitology","topicOriginal":"Medical Parasitology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Pulex irritans"},{"label":"B","text":"Pediculus humanus"},{"label":"C","text":"Ornithodorus spp"},{"label":"D","text":"Dematobia hominis"},{"label":"E","text":"Musca domestica SECTION II: SHORT ANSWER QUESTIONS Diagram"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Parasitology","displayTopic":"Medical Parasitology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"4117e41c32932fc9295f8ff6a2e32d31e47d594d"},{"id":"q-0a233ff95da3","stem":"C___ fish louse","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Anopheles spp."},{"label":"B","text":"Argas persicus"},{"label":"C","text":"Argulus sp."},{"label":"E","text":"Ctenocephalides canis"},{"label":"F","text":"Demodex folliculorum"},{"label":"G","text":"Dermanyssidae spp."},{"label":"H","text":"Dermacentor variabilis I. Gastrophilis intestinalis J. Glossina K. Hypoderma bovis L. Ixodes scapularis (dammini) M. Pediculus humanus humanus N. Pediculus humanus capitis O. Phthirus pubis P. Pulex irritans Q. Sarcoptes scabei R. Simulium daminosus S. Triatoma dimidiata T. Xenopsylla cheopis"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["subject_needs_classification","subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-5d089ffb93d7","stem":"A friend of yours stops by for a visit and tells you that he found a tick embedded in his thigh. He explains that while pulling it out, the “head” broke off and remains in his skin. He was warned by his mom that he should not “leave the head” when removing a tick, and he is concerned about the outcome of this mistake. Please explain to your friend the following (20 total points)","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Why is the term “head” not correct in this context? (3 points)"},{"label":"B","text":"On the back of this sheet, include a ventral perspective drawing of a female Ixodes tick, and label the following structures: hypostome, anus, spiracular plate, pedipalps, carapace (scutum), capitulum and walking legs. (10 points)"},{"label":"C","text":"Explain to your friend how to determine if this is a “Lyme Disease tick”. Include the appropriate structure(s) on your drawing. (3 points)"},{"label":"D","text":"Explain how your friend should have removed the tick. (4 points) MULTIPLE CHOICE QUESTIONS Mark the most appropriate answer for each question listed below on the appropriate answer sheet. (2 points/question)"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","subject_needs_classification","subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"99b4e090866f48c7e08b8a3b0a308973173c8a55"},{"id":"q-a22abb39d690","stem":"Identify the true statement","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"since the lumen of the intestine is considered to be outside the body, tapeworms are considered to be ectoparasites"},{"label":"B","text":"a pack of wolves are described as being in a heterogenetic association"},{"label":"C","text":"within the intestine of most host animals, the oxygen concentration is low"},{"label":"D","text":"the existence of \"life-cycles\" is restricted to parasitic organisms"},{"label":"E","text":"male ticks do not take blood meals MATCHING WORD BANK FOR MATCHING"},{"label":"A","text":"Adult stage"},{"label":"B","text":"African Sleeping Sickness"},{"label":"C","text":"Anal groove"},{"label":"D","text":"Anthelminthic"},{"label":"E","text":"Antibody"},{"label":"F","text":"Antigen"},{"label":"G","text":"Antigenic Variation"},{"label":"H","text":"B-cell I. Bots J. Capitulum (gnathosoma) K. Chagas Disease L. Chelicerae M. Chiggers N. Commensalism O. Complement P. Ctenidium Q Definitive R. Density S. Ectoparasite T. Endoparasite U. Endemic V. Epidemic W. Exoskeleton X. Facultative Parasite Y Host Z. Hypostome AA. Hysterosoma BB. Idiosoma CC. Immunity DD. Incidence EE. Intensity FF. Intermediate GG. Larvae HH. Lice comb II. Lyme's Disease JJ. Macrophage KK. Maggot LL. Malaria MM. Malathion NN. Mange OO. Masking PP. Mutalism QQ. Myiasis RR. Nit SS. Nymph TT. Opisthosoma UU. Parasitism VV. Parentenic WW. Pedipalps XX. Phoresis YY. Plague ZZ. Plasma cell AB. Predation AC. Prevelence AD. Proboscis AE. Prosoma AF. Proterosoma AG. Prothorax AH. Pupae AI. Pygidium AJ. Pyrethrin AK. Reservoir AL. Resilin AM. Rocky Mountain Spotted Fever AN. Scabies AO. Scutum AP. Siphon.... AQ. Spiracle AR. Stylets AS. Symbiosis AT. Temporary AU. T-cell AV. Thorax AW. Tularemia AX. Typhus AY. Uniramous AZ. Vector BC. Warbles BD. Western Encephalitis BE. West Nile Virus BF. Yellow Fever BG. Zoonosis MATCHING For questions 21-31, match the word with its best definition. (2 points each)"}],"priority":0,"status":"review","flags":["subject_unclassified","topic_generic","too_many_options_possible_merge","duplicate_option_labels"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["duplicate_option_labels","long_option_manual_review","nonunique_option_labels","prior_structural_review_flag","repeated_question_stem","subject_needs_classification","subject_unclassified","too_many_options","too_many_options_possible_merge","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"09cf828910d08ea1da03e9c25d9a886b738795e9"},{"id":"q-adb265891c48","stem":"Diagram the basic immune response to an infectious agent (30 points). The diagram must represent or describe the roles of the following immune components","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"antibodies"},{"label":"B","text":"B-cells"},{"label":"C","text":"helper T-cells"},{"label":"D","text":"macrophages"},{"label":"E","text":"plasma cells"},{"label":"F","text":"compliment"},{"label":"G","text":"cytotoxic T-cells"},{"label":"H","text":"interleukins i. Class II major histocompatibility complex coded protein j. memory cells Parasitology Final Exam Nematodes as well as Comprehensive I. Identify the nematode. (20 points)"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","subject_needs_classification","subject_unclassified","too_many_options","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"d4fd7009d9f00e722f5036ec88514a5e400531cb"},{"id":"q-ffe756b433cc","stem":"list, taking into consideration, degree of pathology, mortality, incidence of infection worldwide, and general misery the","type":"Short Answer","subject":"General Pathology","topic":"General and Systemic Pathology","topicOriginal":"General and Systemic Pathology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"General Pathology","displayTopic":"General and Systemic Pathology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-45958472d568","stem":"Situation requiring more specific screening test (tick the correct statement)","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Community Health and Public Health","topic":"Epidemiology","topicOriginal":"Epidemiology","subtopic":"Epidemiolog","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"If early detection of the disease is critical for improving the cure or survival rate."},{"label":"B","text":"If health care facilities are limited or over loaded"},{"label":"C","text":"If treatment of person for whom a false positive results has been obtained will not overload the health care system."},{"label":"D","text":"If announcement of a false positive diagnosis to a patient will not have psychological complication"},{"label":"E","text":"As the first stage screening when the confirmatory test are expensive"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Community Health and Public Health","displayTopic":"Epidemiology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-34cbda558597","stem":"Spurious association between 2 variables could be done to all of the following except","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Community Health and Public Health","topic":"Epidemiology","topicOriginal":"Epidemiology","subtopic":"Epidemiolog","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Due to selection bias"},{"label":"B","text":"Due to randomization"},{"label":"C","text":"Due to information bias"},{"label":"D","text":"Due to confounding"},{"label":"E","text":"Due to measurement bias"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Community Health and Public Health","displayTopic":"Epidemiology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-371f0ac36ee7","stem":"Which one of the following statements is not correct?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Community Health and Public Health","topic":"Epidemiology","topicOriginal":"Epidemiology","subtopic":"Epidemiolog","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"For a normal distribution curve, changing the mean simply moves the curve up or down the axis"},{"label":"B","text":"Approximately 99% of the values under normal distribution curve fall within three standard deviation of the mean."},{"label":"C","text":"Approximately 95% of the values under normal distribution curve fall within two standard deviation of the mean"},{"label":"D","text":"The standard deviation of a sample is always larger than the standard error"},{"label":"E","text":"The larger the sample the larger the confidence interval for a given confidence level."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Community Health and Public Health","displayTopic":"Epidemiology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-66d440c271e1","stem":"The following are characteristics of a confounder except","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Community Health and Public Health","topic":"Epidemiology","topicOriginal":"Epidemiology","subtopic":"Epidemiolog","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"A risk factor for the outcome"},{"label":"B","text":"Associated with exposure"},{"label":"C","text":"Can be controlled during the design and analysis"},{"label":"D","text":"Is on the causal effect pathway"},{"label":"E","text":"Randomization is one way of controlling unknown confounding factors"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Community Health and Public Health","displayTopic":"Epidemiology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-1fc510fa90d7","stem":"Types of Clinical trials include all the following except","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Community Health and Public Health","topic":"Epidemiology","topicOriginal":"Epidemiology","subtopic":"Epidemiolog","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Effectiveness trials"},{"label":"B","text":"Safety trials"},{"label":"C","text":"Therapeutic trials"},{"label":"D","text":"Medical modeling"},{"label":"E","text":"Prophylactic trials e.g. immunization"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Community Health and Public Health","displayTopic":"Epidemiology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-8e2c5da3444f","stem":"After establishing a statistical significance association between variables the following factors need to be considered to confirm the criteria for a causal inference","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Community Health and Public Health","topic":"Epidemiology","topicOriginal":"Epidemiology","subtopic":"Epidemiolog","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Correlation and regression coefficient should endorse the measures of effect"},{"label":"B","text":"The strength of association is measured by OR and RR"},{"label":"C","text":"There is a biological gradient i.e. dose response relationship"},{"label":"D","text":"The association should not challenge existing theories or knowledge"},{"label":"E","text":"The association follow a time sequence (temporality)"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Community Health and Public Health","displayTopic":"Epidemiology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-526a670eb989","stem":"Medical records are usually used to validate the hospital diagnoses of certain disease. By using this validation process instead of relying on hospital discharge code alone, the researcher is trying to reduce which of the following source of error?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"ENT","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Selection bias"},{"label":"B","text":"Prevalence incidence bias"},{"label":"C","text":"Information bias"},{"label":"D","text":"Surveillance bias"},{"label":"E","text":"Confounding bias"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"ENT","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-beb1ceaebf9c","stem":"Analytic studies include all of the following except","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Community Health and Public Health","topic":"Epidemiology","topicOriginal":"Epidemiology","subtopic":"Epidemiolog","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Intervention studies"},{"label":"B","text":"Cross-sectional studies"},{"label":"C","text":"Case-control studies"},{"label":"D","text":"Retro-spective cohort"},{"label":"E","text":"Field trials"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Community Health and Public Health","displayTopic":"Epidemiology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-2f9f75c0d7af","stem":"Regarding cross-sectional studies (Tick the wrong statement)","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Community Health and Public Health","topic":"Epidemiology","topicOriginal":"Epidemiology","subtopic":"Epidemiolog","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"It is possible to collect information on exposure of interest and potential confounding factors"},{"label":"B","text":"The outcome of interest, potential risk factors and target population should be clearly defined"},{"label":"C","text":"In qualitative studies they are useful in assessing practice, attitude, beliefs and knowledge of a population in relation to exposure of interest"},{"label":"D","text":"The target population means all those who will participate in the Study"},{"label":"E","text":"They aim at determining the frequency of a particular attribute in a defined population at a particular point in time"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Community Health and Public Health","displayTopic":"Epidemiology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-d52ec8df149a","stem":"Regarding sampling (Tick the wrong statement)","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Biostatistics and Research","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"If the sampling frame is based on official statistics some groups may be under represented"},{"label":"B","text":"The sampling unit should be an individual person"},{"label":"C","text":"In order to draw a random sample from the source population we need to have a sampling frame"},{"label":"D","text":"In order to select a sample from the source population we need to decide on the sample design"},{"label":"E","text":"The best approach in sampling is to use the random sampling where chance alone determines who will be included in the sample"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Biostatistics and Research","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-df7c64c1ee2d","stem":"Write short notes on the following","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Community Health and Public Health","topic":"Epidemiology","topicOriginal":"Epidemiology","subtopic":"Epidemiolog","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"A confounding variable"},{"label":"B","text":"Secondary attack rate"},{"label":"C","text":"Informed consent in intervention trial SECTION III - LONG ESSAY (30 MARKS)"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Community Health and Public Health","displayTopic":"Epidemiology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"9577e55ed91faa80da011daa55adfb161cecc611"},{"id":"q-681dfb97a29d","stem":"Define each of the three components of the epidemiological triangle, agent, host and environment and discuss the role of each within the concept of multiple causation of disease.","type":"Essay / Structured Essay","subject":"Community Health and Public Health","topic":"Epidemiology","topicOriginal":"Epidemiology","subtopic":"Measures and Study Designs","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Community Health and Public Health","displayTopic":"Epidemiology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-7ec9b971be98","stem":"Explain and describe the concept of population pyramids. Why are they important to epidemiological analysis on disease in a population?","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Community Health and Public Health","topic":"Epidemiology","topicOriginal":"Epidemiology","subtopic":"Measures and Study Designs","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":true,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Community Health and Public Health","displayTopic":"Epidemiology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-5cb0d4e8f471","stem":"Attributable measures are used by researchers to assess the public health impact of a detrimental exposure, assuming causality. Given data from a cohort study on the incidence of stroke, estimate the attributable risk proportion among exposed (physically inactive). Explain your answer in one sentence. Assume that physical inactivity is causally related to stroke risk (10 marks) |Physical activity level|Did develop a stroke |Didn’t develop stroke |Person-year |Incidence per 1000 p4 | |Active |45 |5,955 |43,200 |- | |Inactive |135 |13,865 |100,800 |- | |Total |180 |19,820 |144,000 |- |","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Neurology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Fill in the blacks in the column of incidence per 1000"},{"label":"B","text":"What is the attributable risk proportion"},{"label":"C","text":"Explain your answer"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Neurology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-dec89437c3fc","stem":"In order to estimate counts and rates of work-related fatalities the Occupational Health Department, Ministry of Health introduced a tick-box on the death certificate to indicate “injury at work”. Classification system against a gold standard (International Classification of Diseases (ICD) death certificate codes designating deaths that occurred during work-related activities. After reviewing a sample of 100,000 death certificates, the investigator reported the following. 1,195 true positives 788 false positives, 97672 true negatives and 345 false negatives. (“Positive” means that the tick box was checked “ negative” indicate that it was not checked. “True” indicates agreement between the tick-box and the ICD code. (25 marks)","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Community Health and Public Health","topic":"Epidemiology","topicOriginal":"Epidemiology","subtopic":"Epidemiolog","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Using the account above, complete the 2 x 2 table below: ICD Classification |Death certificate |Work related |Not related |Total | | | | | | |Work related | | | | | | | | | |Not work related | | | | |Total | | | |"},{"label":"B","text":"What are the sensitivity and specificity of the “injury at work” classification system?"},{"label":"C","text":"What is the positive predictive value? In your own words how would you interpret this value?"},{"label":"D","text":"Based on these data is the death certificate “injury at work” classification system likely to under estimate or overestimate the true number of work-related fatal injuries"},{"label":"E","text":"The use of data from the “tick box” on the death certificates to track work-related mortality trends is an example of which kind of surveillance system (choose one best answer)"},{"label":"A","text":"Active surveillance"},{"label":"B","text":"Passive surveillance"},{"label":"C","text":"Retrospective cohort surveillance"},{"label":"D","text":"Cross –sectional survey surveillance"},{"label":"F","text":"The sensitivity and specificity computed above are quantitative measures of which of the following aspects of death certificate classification of work-related fatalities (Choose one best answer)"},{"label":"A","text":"Reliability of death certificate classification"},{"label":"B","text":"Repeatability of death certificate classification"},{"label":"C","text":"Validity of death certification"},{"label":"D","text":"Attributable risk of work-related classification in death certificate"}],"priority":0,"status":"review","flags":["too_many_options_possible_merge","duplicate_option_labels"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Community Health and Public Health","displayTopic":"Epidemiology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["duplicate_option_labels","nonunique_option_labels","prior_structural_review_flag","too_many_options","too_many_options_possible_merge"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-2c6ca819b26b","stem":"During reproductive Health Survey, women were examined to find out if there were association between bacterial vaginosis and intra-uterine devices (IUD). Two hundred and seventy women using IUD and 250 who were not were examined for the presence of bacterial vaginosis. The results were as follows: 170 of those with IUD were found to have bacterial vaginosis out of 250 women who were not using IUD, 110 were found to have bacterial vaginosis. Basing on the above facts, answer the following questions (25 marks)","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Microbiology","topic":"Bacteriology","topicOriginal":"Bacteriology","subtopic":"Bacterial Pathogens","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"What is the percentage of women using IUD were found to have bacterial vaginosis"},{"label":"B","text":"What is its standard error and its 95% confidence interval? (SE = P(1-P) ) n"},{"label":"C","text":"State the null hypothesis and the alternative"},{"label":"D","text":"Construct a 2 x 2 table showing the number of women with and without IUD who had bacterial vaginosis"},{"label":"E","text":"Calculate x2"},{"label":"F","text":"Calculate the 95% confidence of the difference between two proportion of women with and without IUD who had bacterial vaginosis Use the formulae X2 = N(ad-bc)2 efgh 95% CI = P1 – P2 + 1.96 P1(1 – P1) +P2(1 - P2) n1 n2"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Microbiology","displayTopic":"Bacteriology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-09038557248c","stem":"In one study 5,000 were recruited into a cohort study. At the time of their entry into the study, individuals were classified as exposed or unexposed to a nephrotioxic compound on the basis of the type of job they had at that time. The whole cohort was then followed up for risks of dying from renal failure or cancer. The result is presented below (10 marks) | |Exposure | | |Yes |No | |No. initially at risk |1000 |4000 | |Deaths |15 |30 | |Person years at risk |1800 |7500 | Assuming that on average all deaths occurred in the middle of follow up","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Internal Medicine","topic":"Nephrology","topicOriginal":"Nephrology","subtopic":"Nephro","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Calculate the risk ratio"},{"label":"B","text":"Calculate the rate folio"},{"label":"C","text":"Calculate the disease odds ration"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Internal Medicine","displayTopic":"Nephrology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-046574490b63","stem":"which kind of surveillance system (choose one best answer)","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Community Health and Public Health","topic":"Epidemiology","topicOriginal":"Epidemiology","subtopic":"Epidemiolog","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Community Health and Public Health","displayTopic":"Epidemiology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-8374fa9d3ae2","stem":"Physicians tend to be healthier or at least more health conscious than the general population. For that reason Physicians usually have lower incidence of certain diseases (e.g. Cardio-vascular diseases) resulting in the measure of effect that cannot be acurately generalized to other populations. If in your study the response rate of studied Physicians is 68% how might this affect the results of your study. (Tick the correct statement). (2 marks)","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Community Health and Public Health","topic":"Epidemiology","topicOriginal":"Epidemiology","subtopic":"Measures and Study Designs","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Produce a biased result regardless of the exposure or outcome status of the non-response."},{"label":"B","text":"Produce unbiased estimate if the proportion of exposed and diseased non-respondents is the same as the respondents."},{"label":"C","text":"Produce an unbiased results regardless of the exposure or outcome status of the non-response."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Community Health and Public Health","displayTopic":"Epidemiology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-7b2035b7e93c","stem":"Which one among the following statements related to causal – effect relationship is not correct. (1 mark)","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Ecological data is often used for generating hypothesis and should not be used to infer a causal relationship."},{"label":"B","text":"The correlation between 2 data could be coincidental or irrelevant."},{"label":"C","text":"In general, evidence to support a causal relationship between an exposure and outcome is generally produced in cohort studies."},{"label":"D","text":"Comparative studies like case control cannot provide evidence that an association between exposure and outcome do exist."},{"label":"E","text":"Examination of individual case report may provide information that would allow you to refine your hypothesis."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["subject_needs_classification","subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-1f2deef66afa","stem":"The following statements regarding response rate in a cohort study are correct except: (1 mark)","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"The response rate should not affect the level of confounding in a study."},{"label":"B","text":"Statistical power is a function of sample size a low response rate can reduce the power."},{"label":"C","text":"If participation in a prospective cohort study is related to exposure and/or disease status, then selection bias may be a problem."},{"label":"D","text":"A sub-optimal response rate only increase the power of the study and will not bias the measures of association."},{"label":"E","text":"As a general rule of thumb, response rate should be aimed at 80% or more in Epidemiological studies."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["subject_needs_classification","subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-a9d49d895d54","stem":"A prospective cohort study was conducted in Britain to find out the association between cigarette smoking and lung cancer. A cohort of Physician were followed up for 10 years and analysis were made. Because of the small number of women in the cohort males were the only ones who were analysed. Having a restricted group for analysis will affect the generalizability of the research findings and thus the external validity of the study. Based upon the subgroup which was studied to which population would the results be generalized to maintain a high level of external validity (Tick the correct answer(s)) (3 marks)","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"ENT","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"The entire British population"},{"label":"B","text":"Men of similar age as those found in the analysed cohort."},{"label":"C","text":"Well educated men of a similar age and descent as those found in the analysed cohort."},{"label":"D","text":"All British Male Physicians"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"ENT","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["answer_explanation_mixed_into_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-5489852ff2e4","stem":"You are interested in conducting a multi-centre case-control study looking for risk factors associated with lung cancer. One of the pathologists suggests that you use patients from the cardiac unit or emergency department as controls for the lung cancer cases. You respond that the controls (Tick the correct statement). (3 marks)","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"General Pathology","topic":"General and Systemic Pathology","topicOriginal":"General and Systemic Pathology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Should be selected from the cardiac unit only"},{"label":"B","text":"Should be selected from the emergency department only"},{"label":"C","text":"Should be selected from both the cardiac and emergency departments"},{"label":"D","text":"Should not be selected from either the cardiac or emergency department."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"General Pathology","displayTopic":"General and Systemic Pathology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-6b62c3cad6e2","stem":"The results from your case control study of prostate cancer is as follows: Total cases 400 Total controls 400 Cases who smoke 110 Controls who smoke 98 Cases with high fat diets 180 Controls with high fat diets 115 Cases who drink alcohol (regularly) 195 Controls who drink alcohol (regularly) 200 i. The exposure odds ratio for smoking status is: (5 marks)","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Nutrition and Dietetics","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"(110 x 302) / (290 x 98)"},{"label":"B","text":"(98 x 290) / (110 x 302)"},{"label":"C","text":"(110 x 400) / (98 x 400)"},{"label":"D","text":"(110/400) / (98/400) ii. Based on the results from the case control study of prostate cancer, the risk factor (out of the three investigated) that is most likely associated with the onset of prostate cancer is: (5 marks)"},{"label":"A","text":"Smoking"},{"label":"B","text":"High fat diet"},{"label":"C","text":"Regular alcohol consumption"}],"priority":0,"status":"review","flags":["topic_generic","duplicate_option_labels"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Nutrition and Dietetics","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["duplicate_option_labels","nonunique_option_labels","prior_structural_review_flag","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-efd64a47acf7","stem":"Regarding cross-sectional studies (Tick the wrong statement) (1 mark)","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"They aim at determining the frequency of a particular attribute in a defined population at a particular time."},{"label":"B","text":"The outcome of interest, potential risk factors and target population should be clearly defined."},{"label":"C","text":"It is not possible to collect information on exposure of interest and potential confounding factors"},{"label":"D","text":"It is usually considered as a descriptive study design."},{"label":"E","text":"Qualitative study designs are useful in assessing attitude practice and knowledge on exposure of interest."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["subject_needs_classification","subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-087b778b3af8","stem":"The following are characteristics of a good Epidemiological study except: (1 mark)","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Community Health and Public Health","topic":"Epidemiology","topicOriginal":"Epidemiology","subtopic":"Measures and Study Designs","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Epidemiological studies are usually conducted in a sub-set or sample of individuals drawn from the population of interest."},{"label":"B","text":"A sample estimate of a particular epidemiological measure is unlikely to be equal to the true population value due to sampling error."},{"label":"C","text":"If we increase the sample size we increase the standard error and the sampling distribution will become wider."},{"label":"D","text":"The standard error is a measure of the precision with which our sample value estimate the population value."},{"label":"E","text":"Spread of a distribution can be measured by a quantity called the standard deviation."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Community Health and Public Health","displayTopic":"Epidemiology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-5577abdd463f","stem":"Regarding confidence interval (Tick the wrong statement) (1 mark)","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Biostatistics and Research","topic":"Biostatistics","topicOriginal":"Biostatistics","subtopic":"Statistical Inference","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"A confidence interval from a particular study may or may not include the actual population value."},{"label":"B","text":"If we want to be more confident that our interval include the population value, we change from 95% to 99% confidence interval."},{"label":"C","text":"Changing from 95% to 99% confidence interval we replace z value from 1.68 to 1.96."},{"label":"D","text":"The bigger the sample size the smaller the confidence interval of the sample estimate."},{"label":"E","text":"Confidence interval is a range of values that is likely to cover the true population value but we are still not certain that it will."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Biostatistics and Research","displayTopic":"Biostatistics","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-35fef22a4fb3","stem":"The following statements about exposure and outcome are correct except (1 mark)","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"The term risk factor is often used to describe an exposure variable."},{"label":"B","text":"Data on exposure may be available from census, or medical records, the main disadvantage is that the study is more costly and takes a long time."},{"label":"C","text":"Exposure of interest may be associated with either an increased or decreased occurrence of disease or other specified health outcome."},{"label":"D","text":"Exposure and outcome relationships may be mixed up with the effect of another exposure on the same outcome (confounder)"},{"label":"E","text":"The exposure and outcome of interest are specific to study hypothesis and should always be defined before the study starts."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["subject_needs_classification","subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-8dbcf9d8f069","stem":"Testing the significance and difference between means","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Degree of freedom e) Standard deviation"},{"label":"B","text":"F-ratio f) Standard error of the mean"},{"label":"C","text":"Mean squares g) Standard error of the difference"},{"label":"D","text":"N h) t-test Read the list of terms above. For items (a – h), find the matching term in the above list. Terms in the list may be used more than once or not at all (5 marks)"},{"label":"A","text":"This value is calculated by the formulae Standard deviation/square root N......................."},{"label":"B","text":"The t-test is calculated by dividing the difference between Two groups means by this value.........................."},{"label":"C","text":"This value is calculated in order to assess the significance Of difference between means"},{"label":"D","text":"This value is calculated in order to assess the difference among three or more means."},{"label":"E","text":"This calculation is used in ANOVA to compute F-ratio."}],"priority":0,"status":"review","flags":["subject_unclassified","topic_generic","too_many_options_possible_merge","duplicate_option_labels"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["duplicate_option_labels","nonunique_option_labels","prior_structural_review_flag","subject_needs_classification","subject_unclassified","too_many_options","too_many_options_possible_merge","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization"]},{"id":"q-9c8a885c58f0","stem":"Application of statistical approaches","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Chi-squared f) Regression equition"},{"label":"B","text":"Analysis of variance g) Sensitivity"},{"label":"C","text":"Correlation h) Specificity"},{"label":"D","text":"Incidence I) Transformed score"},{"label":"E","text":"Prevalence j) t-test. Read the situation mentioned below and choose the appropriate statistical approach from the list above (8marks)"},{"label":"A","text":"You have moved to a community and you want to know the total number of cases of Tuberculosis in the community. You call the health department and ask for................................"},{"label":"B","text":"After learning the total number of cases of tuberculosis in the community, you call the health department and ask for number of new cases last year so you ask for the........................"},{"label":"C","text":"Assume you study the effect of diet on cholesterol level what calculation would be made to assess the significance of difference in pre- and post-diet mean cholesterol level......................."},{"label":"D","text":"A colleague conducted a study of (1) a control group (2) a group receiving drug A (3) A group receiving drug B. This friend wants to know what statistics to use to assess the differences among the means for the three groups. Your choice is.............................."},{"label":"E","text":"Another colleague heard that you give good advice regarding statistics and asks you what to use to determine if there is a relationship between scores on a nutrition inventory and number of days for post-operative recovery. Both variables are continuous. You say......................................... should work just fine."},{"label":"F","text":"The test results have just come back from the laboratory for tuberculosis. You want to know what proportion of patients with tuberculosis test positive on this test. You want to know the..........................of the test."},{"label":"G","text":"You are still studying the laboratory test results. Now you want to know what proportion of the people without tuberculosis test negative on this test. What you want to know is the...............................of the test."},{"label":"H","text":"The colleague who studied the relationship between the nutritional scores and the hospital stay found a significant association. Now there is a life style inventory under study. Your colleague claims both inventories are looking promising but they have different means and standard deviations. It would be more convenient if there was a common scale. Can the score be converted to a common scale with 50 as a mean and 10 as standard deviation. Sure you say just use......................................... i) Finally you have time to start your own clinical research. You decide to do a simple study: two categories of treatments (Asprin and no asprin) with two categories of outcome (heart problem and no heart problem). Right away you recognize this to be a clear case for using........................................ SECTION II – SHORT AND LONG ESSAYS QUESTION"}],"priority":0,"status":"review","flags":["subject_unclassified","topic_generic","too_many_options_possible_merge","duplicate_option_labels"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["duplicate_option_labels","long_option_manual_review","nonunique_option_labels","prior_structural_review_flag","subject_needs_classification","subject_unclassified","too_many_options","too_many_options_possible_merge","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization"]},{"id":"q-3ca829f4eca0","stem":"Write short notes on the following (15 marks)","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Measurement errors in Epidemiological studies."},{"label":"B","text":"Informed consent"},{"label":"C","text":"Causal – effect relationship"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["subject_needs_classification","subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-42ad6155f4cf","stem":"The following data represent two continuous Physiological variables collected in a standardized fashion from a group of subjects (No calculations are needed) (15 marks) Individual 1 2 3 4 5 6 Variable A 110 105 115 120 125 130 Variable B 20 22 30 40 50 60","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Physiology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Assume that variable A is systolic blood pressure and variable B the body weight in children. Present the data in appropriate graphical form."},{"label":"B","text":"What statistical test would you use to measure the strength of association between variable A and variable B."},{"label":"C","text":"What type of statistical technique would you use to analyse the effect of body weight on systolic blood pressure what criteria relating to the underlying distribution of the data need to be satisfied before this statistical technique can be employed."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Physiology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-b7489b1648ea","stem":"In a study to find out the average weights of babies born at KCMC i) A sample of 200 babies were sampled. The average weights of these babies was 3.2 kg with standard deviation of 0.36. (5 marks) Find the 95% confidence interval for the estimate of babies weights born at KCMC. ii) Fifty patients suffering from the same condition were allocated at random to treatment A or B. After a certain period those patients were asked if their conditions had improved. The results were presented as follows. (20 marks) Treatment |Outcome |A |B |Total | |Improved |20 |15 |35 | |Not improved |5 |10 |15 | |Total |25 |25 |50 |","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Biostatistics and Research","topic":"Biostatistics","topicOriginal":"Biostatistics","subtopic":"Statistical Inference","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"What is the null hypothesis (2 marks)"},{"label":"B","text":"From the above data, do we have evidence that drug A is better than drug B. (do a statistical significance test) (8 marks)"},{"label":"C","text":"Find the 95% CI of the difference on the proportion (8 marks) Use the formulae: 95% CI = P1-P2 + 1.96 x SE SE = P1(1-P1) + P2(1-P2) n1 n2"},{"label":"D","text":"Is there an association between the answer in (b) and that in (c) (2 marks)"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Biostatistics and Research","displayTopic":"Biostatistics","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-385c88c59b56","stem":"Hundred patients presented at the casualty department with fever, abdominal pain and vomiting for the past 2 days sixty percent of the patients had temperatures greater than 38oc. Eighty per cent of patients with temperatures greater than 38oc had malaria parasitemia and 10% of patients without temperature greater than 38oc had malaria parasite mia as shown below (25 marks) Malaria Parasite |Temperature |Present Absent |Total | |Fever > 38oc | | | |< 38oc | | | | Total | |100 |","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Emergency Medicine","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Fill in the figures in this table"},{"label":"B","text":"What is the sensitivity of temperature greater than 38oc as a marker of +ve malaria parasitemia (clinical malaria)?"},{"label":"C","text":"What is the specificity of temperature greater than 38oc as a marker of clinical malaria?"},{"label":"D","text":"What was the positive predictive value of temperative greater than 38oc as a marker of clinical malaria?"},{"label":"E","text":"What was the prevalence of clinical malaria in this studied group?"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Emergency Medicine","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-31c4e9a74095","stem":"What statistical test would you use to analyze these data.","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["subject_needs_classification","subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-52608d8bdf04","stem":"Unique ultra structural feature of Giardia lamblia is the","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Adhesire disk"},{"label":"B","text":"Cysts and trophozoites"},{"label":"C","text":"Flagella"},{"label":"D","text":"Karyosomes"},{"label":"E","text":"None of the above"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["subject_