 gondii to evade the mammalian immune system is........","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Becoming intracellular"},{"label":"B","text":"Penetrating into privileged sites in the body"},{"label":"C","text":"The process of antigenic variation"},{"label":"D","text":"Masking with host antigens"},{"label":"E","text":"Causing polyclonal stimulation which characteristic does not apply to the Balantidium coli"},{"label":"A","text":"The ceacum and the adjacent portion of the large intestine and small intestine"},{"label":"B","text":"Parasite exists in two stages: trophozoite and cyst"},{"label":"C","text":"It is the only ciliates known to infect man"},{"label":"D","text":"It is also the largest human protozoan."},{"label":"E","text":"Life cycle completed in a single host 50."}],"priority":0,"status":"review","flags":["subject_unclassified","topic_generic","too_many_options_possible_merge","duplicate_option_labels"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["duplicate_option_labels","nonunique_option_labels","prior_structural_review_flag","repeated_question_stem","subject_needs_classification","subject_unclassified","too_many_options","too_many_options_possible_merge","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"1ee88a8f69294dadcee40803973086ce32b4ce7d"},{"id":"q-48ee23e76583","stem":"Which term describes the relationship between flagellated protozoa and termites","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Parasitology","topic":"Medical Parasitology","topicOriginal":"Medical Parasitology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"parasitism"},{"label":"B","t