text":"Adhesive disk ,"},{"label":"C","text":"Entamoeba histolytica"},{"label":"D","text":"Toxoplasma gondii"},{"label":"E","text":"Cytokinesis"},{"label":"F","text":"microgametocytes"},{"label":"G","text":"Merozoites"},{"label":"H","text":"Obligate parasite I. Endodyogeny J. Bradyzoites SECTION III : SHORT ESSAY QUESTIONS"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["subject_needs_classification","subject_unclassified","too_many_options","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-dfb2eea34794","stem":"You are a doctor in a small town and several children come to your practice with diarrhea with loose, foul smelling stools, some vomiting, nausea, anorexia and complaining abdominal cramps. You do stool examinations and treat them appropriately. Later on in the same week two more children come to see you with the same symptoms. After some questioning you find out that they all go to the swimming pool. (4 marks)","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":". What did you find they had? Giardia lamblia, detect cysts or trophozoites in stool"},{"label":"B","text":". How did you treat them? Flagyl (metranidazole)"},{"label":"C","text":"Is there anything that you can do to control this outbreak? Fecal contaminationof pool water, cysts are resistant to chlorination, drain pool, clean, bleach, test for cysts."},{"label":"D","text":"What can you recommend to the pool owner to do about this? In courage general hygiene practice"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"