ion of mucus secretion from the patient"},{"label":"D","text":"_______ Control is maily by destruction of the habitat of the vector"},{"label":"E","text":"_______ Kerandel’s is one of the clinical feature in late stages of the disease."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Parasitology","displayTopic":"Protozoology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-f0633caeb702","stem":"About Amoebiasis","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Parasitology","topic":"Medical Parasitology","topicOriginal":"Medical Parasitology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"________ A disease is associated with poor hygiene"},{"label":"B","text":"________ Liver abscess is the most common extraintestinal amoebiasis"},{"label":"C","text":"________ Amoeboma is more frequently found at the junction between caecum and Rectosigmoid"},{"label":"D","text":"________ Most of people infected with appropriate causative agent develop to disease"},{"label":"E","text":"________ Caused by Entamoeba dispar"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Parasitology","displayTopic":"Medical Parasitology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-558a8c5bbeba","stem":"About Larval parasitic disease","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Parasitology","topic":"Medical Parasitology","topicOriginal":"Medical Parasitology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"________ Spagonosis is caused by Larval fom of multiceps spp"},{"label":"B","text":"________ Taenia saginata is respnsoble for cysticeracosis"},{"label":"C","text":"________ Caenurus cyst do not cause any disease in man"},{"label":"D","text":"________ Myiasis is caused by maggots"},{"label":"E","text":"Can not cause a death"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Parasitology","displayTopic":"Medical Parasitology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-4af04bf62b77","stem":"One of the clinical feature of malaria is anaemia; the cause of anaemia in malaria","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Parasitology","topic":"Protozoology","topicOriginal":"Protozoology","subtopic":"Malaria","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Slow bleeding from congested liver"},{"label":"B","text":"Haemolysis of both infected and non infected RBCs"},{"label":"C","text":"Destruction of deformed RBCs by RESU"},{"label":"D","text":"Suppression of glycogenolysis"},{"label":"E","text":"Dyserythropoiesis SECTION C:"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Parasitology","displayTopic":"Protozoology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-cddb196aec9d","stem":"Explain the life cycle of Malaria parasite in both definitive and intermediate hosts.","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Parasitology","topic":"Protozoology","topicOriginal":"Protozoology","subtopic":"Malaria","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Parasitology","displayTopic":"Protozoology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-56832651cb6d","s