ease","type":"Essay / Structured Essay","subject":"Parasitology","topic":"Helminthology","topicOriginal":"Helminthology","subtopic":"Schistosomiasis","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Parasitology","displayTopic":"Helminthology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-de4d31c07018","stem":"10: (10 marks) (Penalty half a mark for a guess work). . Praziquantel - effective in the treatment of all forms of schistosomiasis, with virtually no side effects T • Oxamniquine - used exclusively to treat intestinal schistosomiasis in Africa and South America T • Metrifonate - effective for the treatment of urinary schistosomiasis T • Intermediate host; The host occupied by juvenile stages of a parasite prior to the definitive host and in which asexual reproduction often occurs.T • Reservoir host: Refers to a host or carrier that harbors disease-causing organisms, without injury to itself and serves as a source from which other individuals can be infected.T • Definitive host: the host in which the sexual reproduction of a parasite takes place T • Vector: An organism, often an insect or rodent, that carries disease. T • The principal means of acquiring the toxoplasmosis infection is either by ingestion of inadequately cooked meat primarily beef, pork and lamb or by contact with feral or domestic cats.T • Cryptosporidium parvum is a vector borne. • Balantium coli is a cestode • Cats are intermediate hosts habor sexual stage for toxoplasma T MATCHING QUESTIONS Match the following by writing the correct letter on the space provided (10 marks each) ____ sporocysts ____ adhesive disk ____ tachyzoites ____Schistosomatidae ____ schizogony","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Parasitology","topic":"Helminthology","topicOriginal":"Helminthology","subtopic":"Schistosomiasis","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"used for attachment by Giardia"},{"label":"B","text":"Gynecophoral canal"},{"label":"C","text":"Toxoplasma gondii SHORT ANSWERS QUESTIONS:"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Parasitology","displayTopic":"Helminthology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-752aebc1ef6a","stem":"Mention three orally acquired helminthic infections","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Parasitology","topic":"Medical Parasitology","topicOriginal":"Medical Parasitology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Ascaris lumbricoides"},{"label":"B","text":"Ancylostoma duodenale"},{"label":"C","text":"Necator americanus"},{"label":"D","text":"Trichuris trichura"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Parasitology","displayTopic":"Medical Parasitology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"13ce7363dca067abb765d4eb0ad15e360d91cdc8"},{"id":"q-e48894e905dc","stem":"How does each of the following nematodes infect its definitive host","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Parasitology","topic":"Medical Parasitology","topicOriginal":"Medical Parasitology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Ascaris lumbricoides fecal oral route"},{"label":"B","text":"Toxoplasma gondii"},{"label":"C","text":"Strongyloides stercoralis >Auto infection >Penetration to the skin >Ingestion of Rhabditiform Larva"},{"label":"D","text":"Cryptosporidium parvum"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[