actice_draft","flags":["subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["subject_needs_classification","subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-740e83913798","stem":"Differentiate between the following with aid of labeled diagrams","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Infective stages of Naegleria and Acanthamoeba spp."},{"label":"B","text":"Infective stages of Ascaris lumbricoides and Strongyloides stercoralis"},{"label":"C","text":"Xenopsylla and Pulex spp."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["subject_needs_classification","subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-910151f2864c","stem":"Describe the life cycle of the following parasites in their intermediate hosts","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Plasmodium vivax"},{"label":"B","text":"Schistosoma spp."}],"priority":0,"status":"review","flags":["subject_unclassified","topic_generic","mcq_missing_options"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["mcq_missing_options","not_enough_options","prior_structural_review_flag","subject_needs_classification","subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-c92fae35ac65","stem":"Describe a direct method for diagnosis of the following parasites- Mention and draw the stages found.","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Wuchereria bancrofti"},{"label":"B","text":"Trichomonas vaginalis"},{"label":"C","text":"Enterobius vermicularis"},{"label":"D","text":"Taenia saginata"},{"label":"E","text":"Hymenolepis nana"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["subject_needs_classification","subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-0a0dab0308f8","stem":"Differentiate between the life cycles of two parasites transmitted to man, one through eating meat and another through eating fish in Egypt.","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["subject_needs_classification","subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-65e56cd23c41","stem":"Differentiate between the following","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Microscopic examination of stools in amoebic and bacillary dysentery."},{"label":"B","text":"Types of lice."},{"label":"C","text":"Types of myiasis."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["subject_needs_classification","subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-af9710f2adb8","stem":"Give an account on","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Infective stages and modes of human infection with Toxoplasma gondii"},{"label":"B","text":"Types of biological transmission of diseases by arthropods. Give an example for each. [pic] Biology 545 HUMAN PARASITOLOGY Sample exam The exam below is simply a sample test, portions of which were given to students in 1995. This sample exam is not meant to be all inclusive. Rather, it should be used only to give you an idea of how I design many of my exams. Be sure that not all information in the course is contained within the body of this sample exam. [pic] HUMAN PARASITOLOGY (BIOLOGY 545) PROTOZOA (100 PTS) Please note: A species is binomial."}],"priority":0,"status":"review","flags":["subject_unclassified","topic_generic","mcq_missing_options"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["long_option_manual_review","mcq_missing_options","not_enough_options","prior_structural_review_flag","repeated_question_stem","subject_needs_classification","subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"5eb10d2173c4b34e28a435d4106581e6a8c982e5"},{"id":"q-c730cdb29b73","stem":"Please provide the complete life cycle of Trypanosoma gambiense. Label all stages (10 points). Take me home [pic] [pic] Home | Search | What's New | Help | Comments Kansas State University | Biology Division 30 September, 1999 |The flagellates on the left were found in a vaginal smear of a female student (obviously) who complained of | |vaginitis. The trophozoites measured about 25 micrometers long x 17 micrometers wide. What species do they | |represent? | |[pic]Giardia lamblia | |[pic]Pentatrichomonas hominis | |[pic]Trichomonas tenax | |[pic]Trichomonas vaginalis | |[pic] | |The fully sporulated oocyst on the left was from a population of oocysts found following a flotation of a stool | |from an AIDS patient. Oocysts averaged about 8.4 micrometers long x 6.2 micrometers wide. What species is | |represented? |","type":"Clinical Vignette","subject":"ENT","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"ENT","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-55a8069a4402","stem":"|measured about 52 micrometers long x 22 micrometers wide. What species does it represent? |","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["subject_needs_classification","subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-3f6f4054173e","stem":"Amoebiasis is an infection of","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Parasitology","topic":"Medical Parasitology","topicOriginal":"Medical Parasitology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Small intestine"},{"label":"B","text":"Colon"},{"label":"C","text":"Pancrease"},{"label":"D","text":"Payers patches"},{"label":"E","text":"Mesensteric lymph node"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Parasitology","displayTopic":"Medical Parasitology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-713db1ac42c6","stem":"The infective form of amoebiasi is","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Parasitology","topic":"Medical Parasitology","topicOriginal":"Medical Parasitology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"The vegetative form"},{"label":"B","text":"The trophozoites"},{"label":"C","text":"The cystic form"},{"label":"D","text":"The pseudopodia"},{"label":"E","text":"The sporeform"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Parasitology","displayTopic":"Medical Parasitology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-01e35fbdd6d6","stem":"Write short notes on: Loeffler’s syndrome","type":"Essay / Structured Essay","subject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["subject_needs_classification","subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-ce39ef8dc772","stem":"Write short notes on: How is ascariasis diagnosed in humans?","type":"Essay / Structured Essay","subject":"ENT","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":true,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"ENT","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-5dc66a936d6b","stem":"Describe in detail the life cycle of Strongyloides stercoralis","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["subject_needs_classification","subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-3f59f88153ad","stem":"The following data were gathered from the Framingham Heart Study, an ongoing study in the town of Framingham, Massachusetts. In 1972, 1800 men were examined and it was determined that 500 had high blood pressure (HBP). The men were then followed for the next 18 years to determine how many developed cardiovascular disease (CVD) during that time period. One hundred and sixty men were diagnosed with cardiovascular disease; of these 160, ninety were among the 500 that were initially diagnosed with high blood pressure as well. [15 marks] Construct a 2x2 table for these data and enter the relevant labels and data in the appropriate cells: (4 marks)","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"ENT","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"C","text":"Name the appropriate measure of association (2 marks)"},{"label":"D","text":"Calculate the appropriate measure of association and interpret (3 marks)"}],"priority":0,"status":"review","flags":["topic_generic","mcq_missing_options"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"ENT","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["mcq_missing_options","not_enough_options","prior_structural_review_flag","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-b33061875e6e","stem":"19 years 3 0.18 2.6 20+ years 2 0.19 _______ Non smokers 3 0.07 1.0(ref)","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"ENT","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Calculate rate ratio comparing current smokers with nonsmokers, comment (2 pts)"},{"label":"B","text":"Calculate rate ratio comparing ex-smokers who quit at least 20 years ago with non-smokers, comment (2 pt)"},{"label":"C","text":"Calculate rate ratio comparing ex-smokers who quit < 5 years ago with non-smokers (1 pt)"},{"label":"D","text":"What is the public health implication of these findings? In other words, if you were the public health official how will you convey your message to the public regarding lung cancer rates for smokers, those quitting smoking taking into consideration the rates in nonsmokers (4 pts)"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"ENT","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-177f5a55b7e8","stem":"A total of 109 men were studied in order to investigate a possible association between alcohol consumption and gastric cancer. Two groups of patients were studied. One group of men who had been newly diagnosed with gastric cancer at three general hospital was compared with another group randomly selected from male patients who attended surgical outpatient clinics during the same period in same hospitals. Each patient was asked about their history of alcohol consumption, and was categorized according to their weekly alcohol consumption. High alcohol consumption was defined as more than 28 units per week. It was found that 35 men had consumed more than 28 units of alcohol per week. A total of 54 men had gastric cancer, 22 of whom had a high alcohol intake. [15 points].","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"General Surgery","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"What type of study design was this? (2 pt)"},{"label":"B","text":"What are the three advantages and disadvantage of this design? (3 pts) Advantages.............................................................................. Disadvantages......................................................................................................................................................"},{"label":"C","text":"Draw 2 by 2 table and display the results of the study (3 pts)"},{"label":"D","text":"What is the measure of association used with this study design? (1 pt)........................................................................."},{"label":"E","text":"Calculate the measure of association for this study (4 pts)"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"General Surgery","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization"]},{"id":"q-0b7b8ec717f7","stem":"Some clinicians at a district hospital noticed that some infants suffer from long spells of crying due to colic in the first 3 months after delivery. To know more about the problems of infants in Moshi urban, a study was conducted in January to December 2005. The aim was to investigate among other things if maternal smoking habits during pregnancy may had an influence whether the infant got colic. Women of reproductive age, attending 6 of the municipal primary health centers and dispensaries, having infants aged < 3 months and residents in the district for < 6 months were eligible to participate. Interviews were carried out using standardized pretested questions to look at various risk factors that may contribute to colic. Information about presence of colic infants was also collected. Among 515 non-smoking mothers there were 134 infants with colic. Among 124 smoking mothers there were 50 infants with colic [10 points].","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pediatrics and Child Health","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"What kind of study was this? (1 pt)"},{"label":"B","text":"What are the three advantages and weakness of this design? (3 pts)"},{"label":"C","text":"Draw 2 by 2 table and represent the data (3 pts)"},{"label":"D","text":"Calculate the measure of association and interpret the findings (2 pts)"},{"label":"D","text":"Present a brief abstract with aims, methods, results and conclusion from the information given (4)"}],"priority":0,"status":"review","flags":["topic_generic","duplicate_option_labels"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pediatrics and Child Health","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["duplicate_option_labels","nonunique_option_labels","prior_structural_review_flag","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-801591b51b8f","stem":"Study the figure 1, below and respond to the questions below: (10 marks) Figure 1 What kind of study design does the figure above represent?","type":"Image / Diagram Question","subject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"review","flags":["subject_unclassified","topic_generic","requires_visual_review"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":true,"displaySubject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["prior_structural_review_flag","requires_visual_review","subject_needs_classification","subject_unclassified","topic_generic","visual_asset_not_transcribed"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-968afa2fb52b","stem":"In a mass screening of 5,000 women, 25 of these were found to have breast cancer. During the next five years 10 more of the examined women developed breast cancer. Which measures of disease