ment is appropriate where small numbers of patients are involved"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["source answer/boilerplate removed from option E"]},{"id":"q-782a0770effd","stem":"In the treatment of chronic hepatitis B virus","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Microbiology","topic":"Virology","topicOriginal":"Virology","subtopic":"Viruses","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"corticosteroids are always beneficial"},{"label":"B","text":"combined treatment with acyclovir and interferon is more effective than interferon alone"},{"label":"C","text":"40% of patients can be expected to respond to interferon"},{"label":"D","text":"interferon is more effective in the presence of concurrent HIV infection"},{"label":"E","text":"interferon can be associated with a rise in transaminases towards the end of therapy"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Microbiology","displayTopic":"Virology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":["source answer/boilerplate removed from option E"]},{"id":"q-13946323bc3d","stem":"The following conditions may be significantly worsened by concurrent corticosteroid or cytotoxic drug therapy","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"tuberculosis"},{"label":"B","text":"amoebiasis"},{"label":"C","text":"strongyloides"},{"label":"D","text":"giardiasis"},{"label":"E","text":"ascari