d"},{"label":"D","text":"a berry aneurysm is found on angiography more frequently on the vertebrobasilar than on the carotid system"},{"label":"E","text":"the risk of recurrent haemorrhage is maximal at 10-14 days"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["subject_needs_classification","subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["source answer/boilerplate removed from option E"]},{"id":"q-9efe09cf8704","stem":"Infestation of the following parasites may lead to anaemia","type":"OSCE / Practical Station","subject":"Hematology","topic":"Red Cell Disorders","topicOriginal":"Red Cell Disorders","subtopic":"Anemia","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Taenia saginata"},{"label":"B","text":"Ankylostoma duodenale"},{"label":"C","text":"Wuchereria bancrofti"},{"label":"D","text":"Schistosoma haematobium"},{"label":"E","text":"Ascaris lumbricoides"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Hematology","displayTopic":"Red Cell Disorders","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":["source answer/boilerplate removed from option E"]},{"id":"q-01228c15b73f","stem":"Techniques are available for the ante-natal diagnosis of","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Tay-Sach's disease"},{"label":"B","text":"Down's dyndrome"},{"label":"C","text":"haemophilia"},{"label":"D","text":"phenylketonuria"},{"label":"E","text":"spina bifida cystica"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["subject_needs_classification","subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["source answer/boilerplate removed from option E"]},{"id":"q-4209c77fd4db","stem":"In a young man with a four day history of bloody diarrhoea","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"shigellosis is a likely diagnosis"},{"label":"B","text":"the finding of cysts to E. histolytica in the stools confirms a diagnosis of acute amoebic dysentry"},{"label":"C","text":"cholera is a likely diagnosis"},{"label":"D","text":"a negative amoebic fluorescent antibody test excludes a diagnosis of acute amoebic dysentry"},{"label":"E","text":"giardiasis is a likely diagnosis"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["subject_needs_classification","subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["source answer/boilerplate removed from option E"]},{"id":"q-35ba088c1be8","stem":"Recognised features of general paresis (general paralysis of the insane) include","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"tremor"},{"label":"B","text":"dysphasia"},{"label":"C","text":"occaisional -ve cerebrospinal fluid serology for syphilis"},{"label":"D","text":"extensor plantar reflexes"},{"label":"E","text":"muscular weakness"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["subject_needs_classification","subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["source answer/boilerplate removed from option E"]},{"id":"q-0f1cb34ebb21","stem":"A broad complex tachycardia is more likely to be supraventricular tachycardia with abberation than ventricular tachycardia if","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"cannon waves are seen in the neck waves"},{"label":"B","text":"fusion beats are seen on the ECG"},{"label":"C","text":"the tachycardia is abolished by carotid massage"},{"label":"D","text":"a QS wave is seen in V6"},{"label":"E","text":"there is a concordant pattern across the precordial leads"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["subject_needs_classification","subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["source answer/boilerplate removed from option E"]},{"id":"q-c66607a3d0b7","stem":"Ostium secundum atrial septal defect","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"often leads to atrial fibrillation during the second decade"},{"label":"B","text":"is associated with left axis deviation on the ECG"},{"label":"C","text":"is associated with mitral valve prolapse"},{"label":"D","text":"accounts for the majority of cases of ASD"},{"label":"E","text":"is generally thought to require surgical correction if the pulmonary blood flow is greater than twice the systemic"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["subject_needs_classification","subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["source answer/boilerplate removed from option E"]},{"id":"q-48fab1bc4b75","stem":"In aplastic anaemia","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Hematology","topic":"Red Cell Disorders","topicOriginal":"Red Cell Disorders","subtopic":"Anemia","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"a history of preceding Hepatitis A is associated with a relatively benign course"},{"label":"B","text":"immunosuppressive therapy may be effective"},{"label":"C","text":"a leuko-erythroblastic blood picture may be present at diagnosis"},{"label":"D","text":"ferrokinetic studies (Fe59) show predominant accumulation in the liver"},{"label":"E","text":"a positive Ham's test may be present"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Hematology","displayTopic":"Red Cell Disorders","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":["source a