_unclassified","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["source answer/boilerplate removed from option E"]},{"id":"q-1dcfbe7dc4ed","stem":"A young woman develops malaise, anorexia, sore throat and tender swelling of each side of the neck, for which she takes a week off work. Ten days later her voice assumes a nasal quality, and fluid regurgitates through her nose. She also finds difficulty in reading though distant vision is unaffected.","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"ENT","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Bulbar poliomyelitis has developed through a portal of entry in the tonsillar region"},{"label":"B","text":"there is a particular risk of sudden circulatory failure"},{"label":"C","text":"there is paresis of the soft palate"},{"label":"D","text":"bilateral central scotomas will be present"},{"label":"E","text":"she would be liable to develop a symmetrical weakness and paraesthesia of the limbs within the next week or two"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"ENT","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["source answer/boilerplate removed from option E"]},{"id":"q-3eafea8bc8f9","stem":"Albright's disease of bone (fibrous dysplasia) typically produces","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"osteitis fibrosa disseminata"},{"label":"B","text":"low output failure"},{"label":"C","text":"pigmentation"},{"label":"D","text":"precocious puberty"},{"label":"E","text":"convulsions"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":