ory deficit"},{"label":"B","text":"the severity of intellectual impairment"},{"label":"C","text":"the severity of any personality change"},{"label":"D","text":"the severity of any physical injury"},{"label":"E","text":"the period of retrograde amnesia"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Emergency Medicine","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["source answer/boilerplate removed from option E"]},{"id":"q-0e8a43996ba2","stem":"In which of the following conditions are infantile body proportions seen in a 5 year old child?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pediatrics and Child Health","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Malnutrition"},{"label":"B","text":"Osteogenesis imperfecta"},{"label":"C","text":"Untreated congenital hypothyroidism"},{"label":"D","text":"Achondroplasia"},{"label":"E","text":"Down's syndrome"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pediatrics and Child Health","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["source answer/boilerplate removed from option E"]},{"id":"q-fdb7f3de006f","stem":"In obsessional neurosis","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"patients have good insight"},{"label":"B","text":"patients often give way to their aggressive impulses"},{"label":"C","text":"the occurence of d