"osmolality can be calculated from 2(sodium + potassium) + glucose + chloride mmol/l"},{"label":"C","text":"in ethanol poisoning, the measured osmolality can exceed calculated osmolality"},{"label":"D","text":"one osmole of a substance depresses the freezing point by 1.86°C"},{"label":"E","text":"the main determinant of intracellular fluid osmolality is intracellular potassium concentration"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["short_or_incomplete_stem","subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["short_or_incomplete_stem","short_stem","subject_needs_classification","subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["source answer/boilerplate removed from option E"]},{"id":"q-77899ae564b4","stem":"Cold agglutinins","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"are found regularly in Mycoplasma pneumoniae"},{"label":"B","text":"may produce acute haemolysis in infectious mononucleosis"},{"label":"C","text":"in high titre frequently produce Raynaud's phenomenon"},{"label":"D","text":"commonly produce transfusion reactions"},{"label":"E","text":"are a complication of gonococcal infection"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["subject_needs_classification","subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["source answer/boi